# =============================================================================
# .dockerignore — what must never reach the build context or an image layer
# =============================================================================
# A Docker build context is uploaded to the daemon and every `COPY` that does not
# name an excluded path can pull any of it into a layer. Two consequences make
# this file a security control rather than an optimisation:
#
#   1. `node_modules/` here is a macOS/arm64 tree. Copying it into a linux image
#      produces a container whose native bindings are the wrong platform — the
#      same class of failure DEPLOYMENT_PRODUCTION.md §6 records for `npm ci` on
#      macOS. The image installs its own dependencies from the lockfile instead.
#   2. This repository contains verified-sensitive material: `backups/` and
#      `*.dump` hold real database dumps (password hashes, PII), and `evidence/`
#      holds captured verification output that can quote environment values and
#      request bodies. None of it belongs in an image anyone can `docker save`.
# =============================================================================

# ---- dependencies and builds: rebuilt inside the image ----------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
.swc
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- version control and editor state --------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---- secrets: never copied, never baked into a layer ------------------------
# `.env` is gitignored, but a build context is not a git checkout — it is the
# working tree, so the file WOULD be sent and could be copied by a careless
# `COPY . .`. Excluding it here makes that mistake impossible.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
secrets
secret
credentials
credential
*.credentials
service-account*.json
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# ---- sensitive local artefacts: dumps, backups, captured evidence -----------
# These are the files that must never end up in a published image.
backups
db-backups
dumps
evidence
snapshots
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.backup
backup*.sql
uploads
private-storage
logs

# ---- local verification tooling --------------------------------------------
# `.devtools/` contains an embedded PostgreSQL distribution and its data
# directory — hundreds of MB, platform-specific, and absolutely not runtime
# payload. `scripts/dev-postgres.sh` is referenced by the docs, not by the server.
.devtools
scripts/dev-postgres.sh
scripts/verify-seed-failure.sh

# ---- documentation and reports ---------------------------------------------
# Not needed to build or run. If you have a LICENSE file, un-ignore it: the OCI
# image spec expects licensing information to be present in the image.
*.md
*.markdown
*.txt

# ---- tests -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The verification suites run in CI against a real database, not inside the
# image. Excluded so the image cannot be mistaken for a place they are run.
tests
coverage
*.lcov

# ---- OS noise --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
tmp
temp
.playwright-cli
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.npm_cache
